      "id": "1e5e89b3-9e4f-4e56-826a-e2b37fd28368",
      "name": "Note · 51",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 330,
        "content": "## WP · 51 Approval handler (Telegram trigger): what and why\nHandles taps on the cards from WP · 50 and replies to them. **Must be published (active)** so Telegram can reach it.\n1. **Only Noah's chat** (id in *Parse update*) is accepted; anything else is ignored.\n2. **Idempotent:** acts only while the contact is *Awaiting approval*. A double tap or a late tap gets \"Already handled\", never a second email.\n3. **Legal-basis gate:** Email + Consent / Existing relationship / Inbound → **sent** from hello@. Email + *None - draft only* (all article-sourced leads) → **Gmail draft** in hello@ that you send yourself. LinkedIn → the text comes back to you to paste (LinkedIn has no sending API for this).\n4. **Edit:** reply to the card with your own text (first line \"Subject: …\"); that version goes through the same gate as *Chosen variant = Edited*.\n5. **🌐 WEBSITE? answers** (bottom branch): reply with a domain → Companies.Domain (*Manual*) + that company's *Not reachable*/*Check manually* contacts back to *Needs email*. 🚫 No website → Domain source *No website*.\n6. Every outcome writes Status, Chosen variant, final subject/body, Approved/Sent at and an *Approval log* line to Notion, and confirms in Telegram.\nDocs: docs/50-approval.md"
      }
    }
